{"name":"Marshal Blue","hex":"#3e4355","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marshal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A high-ranking officer in the household of a medieval prince or lord, who was originally in charge of the cavalry and later the military forces in general.","A military officer of the highest rank in several countries, including France and the former Soviet Union; equivalent to a general of the army in the United States. See also field marshal."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To arrange  in line for inspection or a parade.","To arrange  in some methodical order."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marshal"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Marshal","blocks":[{"text":"Marshal is a term used in several official titles in various branches of society. As marshals became trusted members of the courts of Medieval Europe, the title grew in reputation. During the last few centuries, it has been used for elevated offices, such as in military rank and civilian law enforcement."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshal","wikidata":"Q111837"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Georges_Scott_-_Portrait_officiel_du_Mar%C3%A9chal_Foch.jpg/500px-Georges_Scott_-_Portrait_officiel_du_Mar%C3%A9chal_Foch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Georges_Scott_-_Portrait_officiel_du_Mar%C3%A9chal_Foch.jpg/500px-Georges_Scott_-_Portrait_officiel_du_Mar%C3%A9chal_Foch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marshal Foch, circa 1920.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeorges_Scott_-_Portrait_officiel_du_Mar%C3%A9chal_Foch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Lord_Mayor%27s_Show%2C_London_2006_%28295538984%29.jpg/500px-Lord_Mayor%27s_Show%2C_London_2006_%28295538984%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Lord_Mayor%27s_Show%2C_London_2006_%28295538984%29.jpg/500px-Lord_Mayor%27s_Show%2C_London_2006_%28295538984%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"City Marshal of the City of London, on duty at the Lord Mayor's Show.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALord_Mayor's_Show%2C_London_2006_(295538984).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/City_of_Las_Vegas_Deputy_City_Marshals_Cars.jpg/500px-City_of_Las_Vegas_Deputy_City_Mars